  abstract = {A d-regular graph has largest or first (adjacency matrix) eigenvalue $\lambda$1 = d. In this paper we show the following conjecture of Alon. Fix an integer d $>$ 2 and a real $\epsilon$ $>$ 0. Then for sufficiently large n we have that "most" d-regular graphs on n vertices have all their eigenvalues except $\lambda$1 = d bounded above by 2$\surd$d-1 + $\epsilon$. Our methods, being trace methods, also bound those eigenvalues below by -2$\surd$d-1 - $\epsilon$.},
