  abstract = {The conditions for the existence of a unique solution of the matrix equation AXB-CXD=E are proved to be that (i) the pencils A - $\lambda$C and D - $\lambda$B are regular, and (ii) the spectra of the pencils have an empty intersection. A numerical algorithm for solving the equation is proposed. The possibility of a least-squares-type solution is briefly discussed. The set of equations (YA-DZ,YC-BZ)=(E,F) is proved to be equivalent to the aforementioned equation, and its solution is also investigated. A numerical algorithm is proposed.},
